# Production deployment configuration for Jump-PropTech
# ====================================================
# This file should be renamed to .env.production and adjusted for your environment.
# 
# DEPLOYMENT OPTIONS:
# Option A: Supabase + Vercel (recommended, simplest)
# Option B: Self-hosted VPS with Railway/Render
# Option C: Full self-hosted (DigitalOcean, etc.)

# ====================================================
# Option A: Supabase + Vercel (recommended)
# ====================================================

# 1. Create a Supabase project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Run: supabase db remote start (or use the Supabase dashboard)
# 3. Copy the connection string from Supabase Dashboard > Settings > Database > Connection string
# 4. Set the following variables:

# PostgreSQL connection string (from Supabase Dashboard)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.abc123.supabase.co:5432/postgres?schema=public

# Supabase project URL (for Vite frontend)
SUPABASE_URL=https://abc123.supabase.co

# Supabase anon key (from Dashboard > Settings > API)
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Supabase service role key (for API server - has full DB access)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6ikpXVCJ9...

# Node environment
NODE_ENV=production

# Session cookie config for production
# Set to true when served over HTTPS
SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=true

# ====================================================
# Option B: Self-hosted (Railway/Render/VPS)
# ====================================================

# If you're hosting your own PostgreSQL:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@hostname:5432/jump_proptech

# For the API server running on Railway/Render:
PORT=8080

# Allowed frontend origin (must match your deployed frontend domain)
WEB_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app

# ====================================================
# Frontend (Vite) - Vite-specific env vars require VITE_ prefix
# ====================================================

# These are automatically picked up by Vite when prefixed with VITE_
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://abc123.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6ikpXVCJ9...

# ====================================================
# Deployment Steps (Option A: Supabase + Vercel)
# ====================================================

# STEP 1: Set up Supabase
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com and create a new project
# 2. Wait for the project to be ready (takes ~2-5 minutes)
# 3. Go to Dashboard > Settings > Database > Connection string
# 4. Copy the connection string (it will look like: postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.xxx.supabase.co:5432/postgres)
# 5. In the Supabase Dashboard, go to SQL Editor and run the schema:
#    pnpm db:sql (or use the SQL editor to run the drizzle schema)
#    - Or: run `supabase db reset` after setting up the CLI
#
# STEP 2: Set up the API server
# 1. Ensure your API server can connect to the Supabase PostgreSQL
# 2. The Express routes use drizzle-orm with the DATABASE_URL
# 3. No code changes needed if DATABASE_URL is set correctly
#
# STEP 3: Set up Vercel
# 1. Go to https://vercel.com and create an account
# 2. Import your Git repository (Jump-PropTech/artifacts/jump-proptech)
# 3. Vercel will automatically detect it's a Vite/React project
# 4. Add the environment variables in Vercel Dashboard > Project Settings > Variables:
#    - DATABASE_URL (from Supabase)
#    - SUPABASE_URL
#    - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#    - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#    - NODE_ENV=production
#    - WEB_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_URL (same as SUPABASE_URL)
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (same as SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
# 5. Click Deploy
#
# STEP 4: Configure the API connection
# 1. After deployment, Vercel will give you a URL like https://jump-proptech.vercel.app
# 2. Set WEB_ORIGIN to that URL in both the .env and Vercel variables
# 3. The API routes will proxy correctly through Vercel's serverless functions
#
# STEP 5: Test the deployment
# 1. Visit your Vercel URL
# 2. Test sign up / sign in
# 3. Create a property, add a tenant, record rent, etc.
# 4. All data should persist in Supabase PostgreSQL

# ====================================================
# Important Notes
# ====================================================

# 1. The Express API routes (in artifacts/api-server/src/) expect a PostgreSQL
#    connection via DATABASE_URL. With Supabase, this is the connection string
#    from the Supabase Dashboard.
#
# 2. The frontend (artifacts/jump-proptech/) uses Vite with environment variables
#    prefixed with VITE_. These are SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.
#
# 3. Session auth uses scrypt + SHA-256. This works the same with any PostgreSQL.
#    The jp_session cookie is set by the Express middleware.
#
# 4. For production, set SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=true when using HTTPS.
#    Also ensure SameSite=lax or Strict is appropriate for your domain.
#
# 5. The embedded-postgres (local dev only) is NOT used in production.
#    Remove or comment out any references to .local/pgdata.
#
# 6. CORS: The API server may need CORS headers updated for your production domain.
#    Check artifacts/api-server/src/middleware/ or the CORS config.
#
# 7. If you need to run drizzle-kit migrations in production:
#    pnpm db:push --config ./drizzle.config.ts
#    (or use the Supabase dashboard SQL editor)

# ====================================================
# Troubleshooting
# ====================================================

# "Connection timed out" or "ECONNREFUSED":
# - Verify DATABASE_URL is correct
# - Ensure the PostgreSQL server allows connections from your IP
# - Supabase requires allowlist IPs in the Dashboard > Network Egress

# "401 Unauthorized" on API calls:
# - Verify SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is correct
# - Ensure WEB_ORIGIN matches your deployed URL
# - Check session cookie is being sent (HttpOnly, Secure flags)

# "Table 'public.users' doesn't exist":
# - Run the schema push: pnpm db:push
# - Or use Supabase SQL Editor to create tables from the drizzle schema